+# Independent review resolution
+
+The review in `C:\Users\pblit\Downloads\textfile (6).txt` found no high-severity defect in the
+core concentration method. It agreed that the unavailable estimated macro `B` matrices, joint
+covariance, model-unit PC paths, and contract measurement operator are production data blockers,
+not reasons to fabricate targets. This branch therefore distinguishes a verified synthetic
+method demonstration from a fail-closed production estimator.
+
+## Findings addressed after the baseline checkpoint
+
+| Review finding | Resolution | Regression evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Expected numerical failures could terminate MH | A narrow identifier whitelist now converts nonfinite model IRFs, macro targets, losses, and path-map numerical failures into rejected proposals; programming/schema errors still throw. | `test_recognized_numerical_failure_rejects_and_chain_continues`, `test_unexpected_objective_errors_propagate_with_context` |
+| Nonzero but rank-deficient proposal factors were accepted | Both the generic MH routine and sampler driver now check numerical row rank. The coordinate-conditioning opt-in authorizes zero rows only, not hidden linear-subspace conditioning. | `test_rejects_rank_deficient_nonzero_proposal_rows`, `test_rank_deficient_custom_proposal_is_rejected` |
+| `rate_tail` assumed an identity selector | The profiler records the last allowed news horizon and the actual support of general `M_F`; `rate_tail` now begins after measurement support, while `rate_after_news` is retained separately. Plot labels use both horizons. | `test_general_measurement_support_defines_rate_tail` and plot smoke tests |
+| HANK/behavioral structural parity was only manual | The automated grid now compares legacy and PC-path kernels for RANK/HANK, seven/nine parameters, and `T=10,12`, plus RANK→HANK→RANK global-state contamination. | `test_structural_parity_pcpaths` |
+| Covariance conditioning was unreported | The loader retains covariance/precision Cholesky factors and reciprocal condition numbers; the loss is evaluated through a Cholesky factor rather than a dense quadratic multiply. | Loader covariance-equivalence tests and profile loss tests |
+| Mode and sampler supports differed | Both drivers use `get_pcpath_parameter_bounds`; parameter 6 is positive and unbounded, and all other upper bounds are `1-1e-13`. | `test_get_pcpath_parameter_bounds` and sampler integration assertions |
+
+The optional defensive suggestions were also adopted where low-risk: `V_path_model` must have
+full numerical column rank, and unknown path-map option names now error instead of being ignored.
+
+## Verification result
+
+MATLAB R2024a passes 67/67 tests with zero failures or incomplete tests. Code Analyzer reports
+zero findings in every new production file except `solve_model_pcpaths.m`; its 31 findings are
+global-variable and copied-kernel warnings inherited from the legacy structural architecture.
+The new automated parity grid is the safeguard against drift in that copied kernel.
