+# PC-path estimator checkpoints and empirical-data boundary
+
+## What this branch proves
+
+The code on `pc-path-method-demo` demonstrates the method without claiming an empirical
+estimate. At every trial structural parameter, it determines the implementing current/news
+wedge sequence from the interest-rate path alone and then evaluates the inflation/output fit.
+The completed deterministic synthetic demonstration is:
+
+```matlab
+addpath(fullfile(repo, 'model_estim'))
+options = struct( ...
+    'SaveOutputs', true, ...
+    'OutputDirectory', fullfile(fileparts(repo), ...
+        'pc_path_method_demonstration'));
+demo = demo_pcpath_rank7_synthetic(options);
+```
+
+It uses the actual RANK structural kernel and jointly estimates all seven structural parameters.
+The demo is labeled `synthetic_only=true` and `production_ready=false`.
+
+The `PathDesign='empirical-v-n174'` variant holds fixed the empirical raw-contract FF2/ED2-ED8
+two-PC loading matrix and generates the unavailable macro `B` from the RANK model at a known
+truth. Timing is exact: FF2 is H=0, ED2 is H=1, and so on through ED8 at H=7, hence
+`M_F=[I_8,0]`.
+
+## What is intentionally still missing
+
+Production estimation remains blocked until a provenance-complete data file supplies:
+
+- estimated macro response matrices `B_pi_emp` and `B_y_emp`;
+- their joint sampling covariance `Sigma_B` (or audited precision);
+- the normalization, units, target order, and covariance metadata required by `pcpaths-v1`.
+
+The empirical rate-path layer is already fixed: `V_path_model` is the frozen raw-contract loading
+matrix, and its measurement operator is the exact quarter-selection matrix above. In the
+population identification audit, `Sigma_B` is deliberately absent; it would be used only as the
+empirical GMM/quasi-likelihood weight matrix.
+
+The rounded PCA eigenvectors in the methodological handoff are not an estimated `B` matrix and
+must not be promoted into a production target. No `pc_targets.mat` is committed.
+
+## Local restore points
+
+Nothing has been pushed. The first verified implementation is permanently named by the local
+annotated tag `pc-path-baseline-2026-08-21` at commit `6ae9a6b`. It passed the original 55 MATLAB
+tests before the independent-review hardening changes.
+
+To start a separate branch from that exact baseline:
+
+```text
+git switch -c pc-path-from-baseline pc-path-baseline-2026-08-21
+```
+
+The hardened stopping point is named by the local annotated tag
+`pc-path-method-demo-final-2026-08-21`. To add the real empirical `B` layer later without
+disturbing the demonstration:
+
+```text
+git switch -c pc-path-add-empirical-B pc-path-method-demo-final-2026-08-21
+```
+
+That tag is also the clean stopping point immediately before the completed seven-parameter
+synthetic output was added. The completed seven-parameter state is named by the local annotated
+tag `pc-path-rank7-demo-2026-08-22`. To continue from it:
+
+```text
+git switch -c pc-path-add-empirical-B-rank7 pc-path-rank7-demo-2026-08-22
+```
+
+The empirical-`V`/synthetic-`B` DGP state is named by the local annotated tag
+`pc-path-empirical-v-dgp-2026-08-22`.
+
+The population H=3-versus-two-PC identification audit is named by the local annotated tag
+`pc-path-h3-identification-2026-08-22`. The preceding empirical-`V` tag remains the clean rollback
+point for replacing synthetic macro targets with an estimated high-fidelity `B` later.
+
+To return to the maintained method-demo branch:
+
+```text
+git switch pc-path-method-demo
+```
+
+These commands create or switch branches; no destructive reset is needed.
+
+The hardened branch passes 77 MATLAB tests. `INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_RESOLUTION.md` maps every review
+finding to its code change and regression evidence.
+
+## Population identification audit
+
+The completed output in `../h3_vs_pc_identification` compares the full path induced by the H=3
+contract with the complete two-PC empirical path span. The scalar design is locally full rank but
+has pronounced weak identification: the second path factor raises the smallest scaled Jacobian
+singular value by
+about 8 times and raises sensitivity along the scalar design's weakest direction by about 12
+times. These gains survive T=100 and T=120 truncations, nearby population truths, centered-step
+halving, and common-start multistart recovery. This is evidence for weak identification—not a
+claim of exact rank failure.
+
+## Intended empirical follow-up
+
+When the high-fidelity objects become available, place the MAT file outside version control (or
+in an approved data store), point `data_file` at it, and let `get_empirical_pc_targets` validate
+the complete contract. The structural objective, mode driver, and sampler should not need a
+synthetic fallback or a code fork. Any macro timing difference between the estimated `B` and the
+model should be handled with an explicit macro measurement operator, not an undocumented
+relabeling of horizons.
