+## Parallel PC-path estimator
+
+This working tree also contains a legacy-preserving estimator that first implements an
+empirical principal-component policy-rate path with current/news policy wedges and then matches
+only the implied inflation and output responses. It does not modify the original joint-fit
+replication estimator.
+
+The main entry points are:
+
+* `model_estim/get_posterior_mode_pcpaths.m`: posterior-mode driver;
+* `model_estim/sample_posterior_pcpaths.m`: objective-handle random-walk MH driver;
+* `model_estim/plot_model_irfs_pcpaths.m`: path, macro-IRF, tail, and conditioning diagnostics;
+* `_auxiliary_functions/map_paths_to_news.m`: exact square path-only solve;
+* `_auxiliary_functions/solve_model_pcpaths.m`: parallel macro-only quasi-posterior objective.
+
+The required MAT-file contract and normalization metadata are documented in
+`model_estim/_data/README.md`. No production PC target file is bundled: exact two-PC macro LP
+coefficients and their joint covariance must be provided before empirical estimation. For the
+FF2/ED2-ED8 design used here, contract row 1 is quarter H=0, row 2 is H=1, and so on, so the
+measurement operator is known exactly as `M_F=[I_8,0]`.
+
+The sampler's default proposal reproduces the legacy convention that holds parameter
+coordinates 3 and 5 (and behavioral coordinate 8) fixed. Because that defines a conditional
+posterior, it requires the explicit option `allow_fixed_parameter_conditioning=true`. To sample
+those coordinates instead, supply a full-row-rank `proposal_factor` that moves them.
+
+### Seven-parameter synthetic method demonstration (no estimated B required)
+
+The concentration logic can be illustrated without pretending that the unavailable empirical
+two-PC macro coefficient matrix is known:
+
+```matlab
+addpath(fullfile(repo, 'model_estim'))
+options = struct( ...
+    'SaveOutputs', true, ...
+    'OutputDirectory', fullfile(fileparts(repo), ...
+        'pc_path_method_demonstration'));
+demo = demo_pcpath_rank7_synthetic(options);
+```
+
+This deterministic demonstration uses the repository's actual RANK structural kernel and jointly
+estimates all seven parameters (`h`, `calvo_p`, `zeta_p`, `calvo_w`, `zeta_w`, `kappa`, and
+`psi_uti`). At every trial vector it recomputes the implementing news basis from the rate block,
+then evaluates the macro-only residual. It writes a completed figure, Markdown report, CSV table,
+and MAT result. The output is marked `synthetic_only=true` and `production_ready=false`.
+
+The older `demo_pcpath_method_synthetic.m` scalar example remains only as a fast unit-level check
+of the concentration algebra. Production mode estimation and sampling remain fail-closed until
+exact empirical `B_pi_emp`, `B_y_emp`, their joint covariance, and associated target metadata are
+supplied.
+
+To replace the synthetic path with the frozen empirical FF2/ED2-ED8 two-PC loading matrix while
+continuing to generate `B` from a known RANK truth:
+
+```matlab
+options.PathDesign = 'empirical-v-n174';
+options.OutputDirectory = fullfile(fileparts(repo), ...
+    'pc_path_empirical_V_dgp');
+dgp = demo_pcpath_rank7_synthetic(options);
+```
+
+This semi-synthetic DGP uses
+`V = diag(contract_standard_deviations) * standardized_eigenvectors` from the documented
+174-announcement PCA sample and the exact H=0,...,7 timing `M_F=[I_8,0]`.
+
+### H=3 component versus two-factor identification audit
+
+`model_estim/diagnose_h3_vs_pc_identification.m` compares a scalar H=3-contract experiment with
+the complete empirical two-factor path span in population. The default truth is the strongest
+eligible point in a deterministic 50-point interior Latin-hypercube screen; it is not obtained by
+optimizing a singular value. Both nine-parameter Jacobians are full rank, but the two-factor
+design raises the smallest singular value by about 8 times and sensitivity along the weakest H=3
+direction by about 12 times. The gain survives longer model truncations and nearby truths.
+
+This diagnostic needs neither an estimated macro `B` nor `Sigma_B`: macro targets are generated
+exactly by the behavioral RANK model, and the losses are population distances. `Sigma_B` enters
+only the empirical GMM/quasi-likelihood weight matrix once an estimated macro `B` is used. The
+completed tables, figures, multistart solutions, and MAT result are saved in
+`../h3_vs_pc_identification`; no command needs to be run to view the demonstration.
+
+Run the extension tests in MATLAB with:
+
+```matlab
+restoredefaultpath
+repo = '/absolute/path/to/mp_modelcnfctls';
+addpath(fullfile(repo, '_auxiliary_functions'))
+results = runtests(fullfile(repo, 'tests'));
+assertSuccess(results)
+```
+
+The hardened method-demo checkpoint passes the complete test suite. See
+`PC_PATH_CHECKPOINT.md` for local restore commands and the precise empirical-data boundary, and
+`INDEPENDENT_REVIEW_RESOLUTION.md` for the review findings and their regression coverage.
+
